%     \item Polynomial contrasts are particularly useful when the treatments are determined by levels of a quantitative variable $X$.
%     \item We looked at a linear contrast, whose coefficients are proportional to $w_i = x_i - \bar{x}$.
%     \item Similarly, there are contrasts that focus on the quadratic, cubic and higher order terms.
